diff --git a/docs/Open_Bugs_RCA.md b/docs/Open_Bugs_RCA.md
index 3e8cc77..b3b3d17 100644
--- a/docs/Open_Bugs_RCA.md
+++ b/docs/Open_Bugs_RCA.md
@@ -375,6 +375,68 @@ fill_cell loop counter preservation.
 
 ---
 
+## BUG-015 🟡 Loop-head cond_ret clobbers the accumulator holding the exit value
+
+**Symptom:** A loop whose condition has a *value* (not a bare comparison flag)
+returns 0 instead of the loop-carried value.
+
+**Reproducer:**
+```nanz
+fun count_and(n: u8) -> u8 {
+    var i: u8 = 0
+    var c: u8 = 0
+    while i < n && c < 3 {
+        c = c + 1
+        i = i + 1
+    }
+    return c
+}
+```
+`count_and(10)` returns 0 on Z80; the MIR2 VM returns 3.
+
+**MIR2 is correct** — the join carries the condition value and the exit
+value separately:
+```
+block @cond_join6(%r96: bool [general]):
+  %r98 = cmp.ne %r96, %r97 : bool [flag]
+  cond_ret %r98, [%r87], @loop_body2()   ; %r87 = c
+```
+
+**The Z80 output loses the exit value:**
+```z80
+.count_and_cond_join6:
+    LD A, E
+    AND A
+    RET Z        ; hands back A = the condition value (0), not c
+```
+
+**RCA:** The allocator places the exit value `%r87` in A, so
+`buildReturnCopies` emits no copy and the `TermCondRet` emitter takes its
+`thenFT && len(retCopies) == 0` shortcut (`z80codegen.go:6851`), assuming the
+return value is already in A. But the condition's own materialisation
+(`cmp.ne %r96, 0` → `LD A, E / AND A`) has just overwritten A. `saveAccForCondRet`
+exists for exactly this hazard and does not fire for this shape.
+
+**Baseline reachability:** The eager (non-short-circuit) `&&` the MinZ frontend
+lowers reaches the same hazard with a different symptom — an unencodable `LD`
+at the join. Verified on `85bf008`, so this is not specific to the Nanz
+short-circuit lowering; the new lowering only makes it reachable from Nanz.
+
+**Fix options:**
+1. Widen `saveAccForCondRet` to any `TermCondRet` whose return-value locs
+   overlap a loc the condition materialisation writes.
+2. In the `len(retCopies) == 0` shortcut, verify the value's loc has not been
+   written since its last assignment before taking the `RET cc` form.
+
+**Priority:** Medium. Loops with plain comparison conditions are unaffected;
+value-valued conditions (logical operators, materialised `!=`) that carry a
+live value out of the loop are.
+
+**Discovered:** 2026-10-24, while wiring short-circuit logical operators for
+Nanz.
+
+---
+
