+# Short-circuit logical operators for Nanz — 2026-10-24
+
+`&&` and `||` now work in Nanz (and therefore in `.minz`, which routes through
+the same parser — `cmd/minzc/main.go` handles `case ".nanz", ".minz"`). They
+short-circuit: the right operand runs only when the left one demands it, so a
+side effect in it is conditional.
+
+```nanz
+fun is_alpha(c: u8) -> bool {
+    return (c >= 65 && c <= 90) || (c >= 97 && c <= 122)
+}
+
+if flag && note(true) { ... }   // note() runs only when flag is true
+```
+
+**Baseline for this report:** `85bf008`. All changes are in the working tree
+(`minzc/pkg/nanz/parse.go`, plus docs and tests); nothing is committed yet.
+
+## What landed
+
+Four pieces, all in `pkg/nanz/parse.go`:
+
+1. **Lexer.** `tokAmpAmp` / `tokPipePipe`, emitted before the single-`&`/`|`
+   and `|>` cases so `a && b` is one operator, not two.
+2. **Precedence.** The `binops` table was renumbered to leave room for the two
+   new levels and now follows C's chain exactly:
+
+   | Level | Operators |
+   |-------|-----------|
+   | 10 | `*` `/` `%` |
+   | 9 | `+` `-` |
+   | 8 | `<<` `>>` |
+   | 7 | `<` `<=` `>` `>=` |
+   | 6 | `==` `!=` |
+   | 5 | `&` |
+   | 4 | `xor` |
+   | 3 | bitwise OR |
+   | 2 | `&&` |
+   | 1 | logical OR |
+
+   (`xor` moved from 2 to 4, staying between bitwise OR and `&` as before.
+   The pipe-containing rows are spelled out in words here; `docs/Nanz_Language_Book_v2.md`
+   §2.8 has the escaped table.)
+3. **Desugar at parse time.** In `parseBinary`, `&&` and `||` build an
+   `hir.CondExpr` instead of a `BinExpr`:
+
+   ```
+   a && b  →  if a { bool(b) } else 0
+   a || b  →  if a { 1 } else bool(b)
+   ```
+
+   `CondExpr` lowers to a `BrIf` with one block per branch, so the right operand
+   — and its side effects — only execute on the taken branch. No new MIR2
+   instruction, no new pattern, no new register constraint: the short-circuit
+   semantics ride on control flow the backend already knows.
+4. **Canonical results.** `parser.boolValue(e)` coerces an operand to a real
+   `1`/`0`. Only bool literals, `0`/`1` int literals and *bool-typed* variable
+   references pass through unchanged; anything else — a comparison, a bool-returning
+   call, a non-bool scalar, a nested if-expression — is wrapped in a
+   `CondExpr` that yields the constants. This matters because the Z80 backend
+   materialises a comparison flag as `0xFF`: leaking the operand instead of
+   the value would hand back `255` where a `bool` was promised.
+
+One parser bug surfaced on the way and is fixed by the same change: the
+tuple-vs-paren disambiguation in `parseReturn` consumed the `)` of a
+parenthesised return and **stopped there**, so `return (x & (1 << b)) != 0`
+died with `unexpected token "!="`. It now hands the already-parsed group to a
+new `parseBinaryTail`, so the surrounding binary expression continues.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- **New tests** (`pkg/nanz/logical_e2e_test.go`, 248 LOC):
+  - `TestLogical_Precedence` — 8 shapes, including 4 that must *not* move:
+    comparisons inside `&`, arithmetic inside `|`, arithmetic inside shifts,
+    `*` inside `+`.
+  - `TestLogical_Asserts` — 40 asserts: 36 on the MIR2 VM, 4 also on the Z80
+    emulator (`bool_ops`, `and_bool`, `or_side`, `is_alpha`). Covers short-circuit
+    side effects, non-bool operands, nested logicals, logicals as `while`
+    conditions, and the bitwise operators.
+  - `TestLogical_ReturnParen` — 3 asserts for the `return (a && b) || …` shape.
+- **All three pass:** `go test -count=1 -v -run TestLogical ./pkg/nanz`.
+- **Corpus sweep** (160 source files, default options): **101 → 103** of 160
+  compile. Exactly three lines differ from baseline:
+  - `examples/bit_manipulation.minz` — was `unexpected token "!="` at line 15,
+    now compiles (the `parseReturn` fix).
+  - `examples/feature_tests/01_basic_types.minz` — was a lambda misparse at line
+    43 (`if !(t && t) …`), now compiles.
+  - `examples/glsl2_csg_demo.minz` — was `unexpected token "*"` at line 31
+    (`return (a >> 4) * (b >> 4)`), now reaches its real gap: `unknown type "vec2"`
+    at line 122.
+- **No regressions.** The `TestShowcaseCompileAssemble` failure set is
+  byte-identical to baseline (38 files, same names). `pkg/abap` (2) and
+  `pkg/mir2gpu` (3, GPU hardware) fail on baseline too — checked by stashing
+  `pkg/nanz/parse.go` and re-running.
+- **New example** `examples/nanz/logical_short_circuit.nanz`: 10 Z80-emulated
+  asserts plus 3 MIR2-only. It compiles clean, and `scripts/validate_corpus.sh`
+  reports 0 Z80-VALIDATE errors.
+
+## Known gaps, both pre-existing
+
+1. **`--lir` miscompiles the CondExpr family.** Under `--lir`,
+   `is_alpha(97)` returns 0 — the emitted join compares the *constant*
+   (`LD A, 65 / CP 65`) instead of the parameter. It is not specific to this
+   lowering: on `85bf008`, `examples/c89/logical.c` (which has always produced
+   `CondExpr`) fails the same way —
+
+   ```
+   mz examples/c89/logical.c --lir --asserts-force z80
+   → assert is_printable(65) [z80]: got 0, want 1
+   ```
+
+   Production (`PBQP+Z80Codegen`) is unaffected, and `--lir` is not the default.
+   LIR is 🚧 WIP; this is one more entry in its unfinished CondExpr story.
+2. **BUG-015** — a loop whose condition has a *value* (here: the result of
+   `&&`) clobbers the accumulator holding the loop's exit value, so
+   `count_and(10)` returns 0 on Z80 while the MIR2 VM returns 3. Registered in
+   `docs/Open_Bugs_RCA.md` with RCA: `TermCondRet`'s
+   `thenFT && len(retCopies) == 0` shortcut assumes the return value is already
+   in A, and the condition's own materialisation (`cmp.ne x, 0` → `LD A, E /
+   AND A`) has just written A. Baseline reaches the same hazard through the eager
+   `&&` the legacy MinZ frontend lowers, with an unencodable `LD` as the
+   symptom. The example and the e2e test keep that function on the MIR2 VM
+   only, and say so in a comment.
+
+## One divergence worth following up
+
+The legacy MinZ frontend lowers `&&` **eagerly** (`%r11 = and %r7, %r10` —
+both operands always evaluated), while Nanz now short-circuits. Same spelling,
+different semantics in the same repository. The MinZ path also mis-parses
+`c < 3` into `addr_of @c` in that dump, so its logical lowering deserves a
+review of its own; out of scope here.
+
+## Docs touched
+
+- `docs/Nanz_Language_Book_v2.md` §2.8 — corrected precedence table, new
+  §2.8.1 on short-circuit semantics; §2.14 notes that `&&`/`||` are not
+  overloadable (they desugar in the parser, so there is nothing to short-circuit).
+- `docs/Open_Bugs_RCA.md` — BUG-015 entry and summary-table row.
